// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// A Measure's FIRST unit must be the canonical one, marked with a leading '*'. This file
// declares two perfectly well-formed units and no canonical marker.
//
// Measure is the least-written element in the language and therefore the one whose rules a
// rewrite is most likely to reconstruct from a single example. The '*' looks like emphasis
// on one arbitrary member of a list -- it is in fact structural: the canonical unit is a
// separate grammar slot, mandatory and singular, and everything else is the repeated tail.
###Pure
Measure fixture::neg::NoCanonical
{
   Gram: x -> $x;
   Kilogram: x -> $x * 1000;
}
